\f1\fs22 During the next almost-three weeks, Sarah and Tony enjoyed some quality time together, even if they were bored out of their minds when they weren\'92t uneasy about how safe and sinister the days and nights were. Safe, because they were beset on all sides by no PAPER agents, nightclub bombers, Public Affairs police officers, prophecy facilitators, nor insidious granny fashion-diva arms dealers. Sinister, because the lack of villains was due to: squadrons of GI Blues series Elvi, male and female, patrolling 24-7 the grounds, the perimeter, the hallways, the rooftops, the badly sealed windows, the peanut butter cellar and underneath Sarah\'92s bed, and the battalion of tanks that sat like titanic cane toads out side the gates and at strategic cross-roads through out the neighbourhood.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Perhaps the worst of it was if the Elvi assumed Tony was the father of the evil nematode squatting in her uterus. At first, Sarah assumed they\'92d expect them to sleep in the same bed, but the Elvi proved to be Catholically opposed to any carnal insinuations regarding the Holy Momma. Where Tony slept was anyone\'92s guess and Sarah wasn\'92t asking. Although she wondered if he was still wearing those fairy boxer shorts.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>When Sarah wasn\'92t bored, she was impatient which, if we are to accurately reflect the history of this story, was a high percentage of her waking nano-seconds, and at least half of her nightmares. When the forty-second day since the night of her probable insemination came and went, Sarah feared Kathy would never return, and she would have to call upon another incarnation of Doctors John and Nick in the hope they may know what a DNA test was.\
\pard\pardeftab360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

