\f1\fs22 Kathy arrived on the forty-third day.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With half a breakfast burrito in his hand and some of it on his face, Tony padded in bare feet and flannel pyjama bottoms to meet the doorbell. An Elvi guard, of course, beat him to it, opened the door and greeted a preternaturally smiling doctor toting sewing-machine-sized piece of medical equipment. They exchanged some words, and the doctor tossed the Elvis a patch like it was a floppy ninja throwing-star.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Do 
\f3\i not 
\f1\i0 use that with amphetamines,\'92 Kathy cautioned.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi led Kathy up the staircase; Tony followed a dozen steps behind.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy knocked at Sarah\'92s door, announced herself and was admitted by a muffled come in. She shut the door in Tony\'92s face, leaving him floating in fetid lagoon of hope and apprehension.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi took up guard at the door. He sniffed and sneered at Tony. \'91What\'92s in that?\'92 the Elvi interrogated with a degree of disdain for Tony\'92s meal.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony swallowed. \'91Barramundi.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91With onions?\'92 The Elvi became agitated.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sure. Want some?\'92 Tony waved the burrito at the Elvi, who gagged and put his hand over his nose and mouth.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Nancy!\'92 the Evli called.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony could hear, mutterings of, \'91Oh dear, oh dear,\'92 approaching at top housekeeper speed. Nancy appeared, advanced on Tony and seized his breakfast.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Hey!\'92 he protested.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Nancy vigorously wiped Tony\'92s mouth with a tea towel. \'91No, fish 
\f3\i or
\f1\i0  onions in this house,\'92 she said while scouring every mop of sauce from his face. After assessing Tony\'92s appearance was minimally satisfactory, she withdrew.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The door opened abruptly. Kathy stood blocking the way, holding a syringe up like a candle. \'91Blood sample,\'92 she said to Tony.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony licked his fingers.\
\pard\pardeftab360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

